{
 "name": "tiger_ye_shrine",
 "_brief": "V-B 神像虎: a Taiwanese temple Tiger Lord CARVED AS A SHRINE STATUE. Seated bolt upright on his haunches like the stone tiger under the altar table, chest thrown out, front legs two straight pillars, right forepaw planted on a gold coin. Square block head held high and level, heavy carved browridges, gold seal on the brow, gold eyes, a red sash crossing the chest in a V with a big gold plaque at its point. Feel: sacred, solemn, unmoving authority — a god's guardian, NOT an animal caught mid-stride. Signature = the red sash V + gold plaque. Identity view = side.",
 "_exaggeration_vs_anchor": "wolf anchor W/H 1.41 -> push the OTHER way to ~1.05 (a vertical column, not a long low quadruped); leg_fraction 0.35 -> ~0.42 (front legs are pillars carrying the whole body); head held at the very top of the mass instead of out front.",
 "_paw_note": "buildPaw 的預設 offset 會把腳掌吸到地面；踩在金錢上的右前掌必須自己給 offset。",
